    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0456" n="382" xml:id="pg382"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Clay</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 3, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir:</hi> I have received your kind letter of
                    the 25th April last, in which you speak of the future of our country, and I have
                    to thank you for your suggestions concerning the principles with which we should
                    be controlled. While seriously affected by what you communicate, and while
                    cordially agreeing with you, I am yet in too feeble a state of health to answer
                    you otherwise than through an amanuensis.</p>
                <p>I am, my dear sir, very faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassius M. Clay,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
